#: src/ui/views/advanced.rs:227
msgid "When you start a video or voice call, your Bluetooth headset can switch to a special call mode that turns on the microphone — but the sound becomes mono and lower quality, like an old phone. This is off by default so music and movies stay in full quality even when an app asks for the microphone. Turn it on if you rely on the headset's microphone for calls."
